Jistan Idiot <jistanidiot@gmail.com> wrote:
> So another rainy weekend finds myself trying to add something to my
> version of nethack.
> 
> I've managed to create individual levels and even created a new
> branch.
> The main sources of help have been:
> http://members.shaw.ca/rob.ellwood/sources.txt
> http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Des-file_format
> http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Dungeon.def_format
> http://nethack.wikia.com/wiki/Makedefs
> 
> I have some questions.
> 
> 1) What's the difference between the alters?  sanctum seems to be used
> in Gehennom and Astral.  I think shrine is used in mintown. Altar I
> assume is just a plain old random altar.  sanctum vs shrine my guess
> is no convert vs convert allowed.

Sanctum has High Priest in attendance, shrine has aligned priest.

> 2) Is it possible to create a no gravity zone like the plain of air?
> Is it possible to confine it to one particular part of the map?  If so
> how?

No, the no-gravity is hardcoded to the plane of Air.

> 
> 3) is it possible to only allow specific monsters to be randomly
> generated on the level?  If I only want water elementals and ghosts on
> the level how would I do that?

No. (Except Quest levels, and there the monster generation is hardcoded
to the class quest enemies [include/you.h, Role-struct, enemy*-fields])

> 
> 4) It was recommended in another thread to use "make all" and "make
> update" when adding branches and levels and stuff.  However it appears
> that they completely ignore mybranch.des.  If I manually run lev_comp
> and generate the .lev files, "make all; make update" doesn't copy them
> over to the nethackdir.  Also if I make changes to dungeon.des "make
> all; make update" doesn't catch it.  I have to manually run makedefs -
> e then dgn_comp dungeon.pdf and then copy the dungeon file over to
> nethackdir.  Is there someway to fix this?

Yes. Edit the Makefiles. (Probably just dat/Makefile, and
spec_levs-part of that)

> 
> 5) I have discovered that if I have the flag hardfloor for a level,
> that i can't have holes even if I define a trap in the .des file.  Is
> there some way to have an undiggable floor with holes and trap doors
> similar to the castle?  I suspect the castle works b/c it is the
> bottom of the dungeon.

The castle is hardcoded to allow holes, otherwise no.
(See Can_fall_thru() in src/dungeon.c)

> 
> 6) Dungeon names, how long can they be?   It seems that when I name my
> branch "The Tower of the Ultimate Doom" everything seems to compile
> but the game crashes with the error find_level can't find it.  However
> if I call it "T o t U D" all is good.

23 or 24 characters. (Though dgn_comp allows arbitrarily long names;
this seems like a bug, and should be reported to the devteam.)

> 
> 7) Irregular temple boundaries when two or more temples are touching.
> The priest doesn't greet  you when moving between temples.  In the
> below example they only greet you if you enter from either the left or
> right door.  The middle door they act like you're already there. I've
> tried a lot more B in the space between but that didn't work either.
> Adding more walls and a door is the only thing that works.
> (fixed width font is needed below)
> ...|------------| |----------------|..
> ..|-............-|-................|..
> ..+.............B+B................+..
> ..|-............-|-................|..
> ...|------------| |----------------|..
> 

Hm, quickly eyeballing through the source, this may be a bug.
(src/priest.c, intemple() uses u.urooms0 to check whether the temple
is occupied, but I think it should use u.urooms. No, I haven't tested this)

> 
> 8) If I want to add another ceremony similar to the Invocation ritual
> in order to enter my new level, will that require some C coding?

Correct.

